<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="041" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-18: Job B "Submit as request (type)" proposal kind at non-intake mailboxes — Accept creates request + run under the confirming user; Dismiss audited; never automatic</title>
    <phase>2 Email and Copilot doors</phase>
    <gate>after:029,040</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tag bff-api; modifies the Job B proposal producer and apply service (.cs) on a user-impersonated write path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extends an impersonated, ArchTest-guarded write path (`CommunicationProposalApplyService` is a pinned `ConfirmedProposal` caller) shared with the email-intelligence projects; a mistake creates requests without confirmation or breaks existing field-update proposals.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>reads the intake flag added by task 040 (must run after it); no file overlap with 042–044.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>029, 040</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, backend, ai, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a new Job B proposal kind, "Submit as request (type)", to the existing review queue. At non-intake mailboxes, when the existing `CommunicationTriageAi` result signals a request (no extra AI call), the Job B propose step writes one such proposal per communication. Accept (through `CommunicationProposalApplyService.ApplyAsync`) creates the request and run under the confirming user via task 022's `IntakeRequestSubmitService`; Dismiss writes the existing single Dismissed audit row. Nothing is ever created without an Accept, and existing field-update proposals behave unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the email-intelligence Job B pipeline (`CommunicationEnrichmentService`, `CommunicationProposalApplyService`, `sprk_emailreviewlog`) and ADR-028 A5 impersonation. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The propose step emits the new kind only for non-intake mailboxes with a request signal; Apply and Dismiss handle it with the existing guards; the queue feed carries it in the existing `QueueFeedItem` shape; tests prove the four FR-18 cases.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-18 (a–d); owner reuse decision (2026-11-25): extend the Job B proposal queue, triage supplies the signal (reuse-scan row 9). Job B proposals are `sprk_emailreviewlog` rows (target entity/field/record, `sprk_action`) written by `CommunicationEnrichmentService.RunEmailProposeAsync` (:881, called :243 with the triage result) and resolved by `CommunicationProposalApplyService` (ApplyAsync :169 — resolves the caller fail-closed, loads the row, refuses an already-resolved row; DismissAsync :354 writes one Dismissed row). The queue feed is `GET /api/communications/queue-feed` (`CommunicationEndpoints.cs:382`). The intake flag comes from task 040; intake mailboxes already create requests, so they get no proposal.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (RunEmailProposeAsync :881)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs (ApplyAsync :169, DismissAsync :354, resolved-state guard ~:626)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (queue-feed projection :382 — only if the new kind needs a label field)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplySeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Communication/SubmitAsRequestProposalTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ICommunicationTriageAi.cs (CommunicationTriageResult :82 — Category, Summary, Obligations, Priority, ReviewOutcome)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitService.cs (task 022)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (UpdateRecordAsync remarks: pinned ConfirmedProposal callers, ArchTest ActionSeamUpdateRecordCallerGuardTests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="029" status="pending">Phase 1 on dev; `IntakeRequestSubmitService` (task 022).</dependency>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">Intake flag on the communication account.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">SCOPE = the propose step. No new AI call and no new Action: the kind is derived only from the existing triage result already passed to `RunEmailProposeAsync`; if triage is null (Null-Object or failure), no proposal of this kind is written.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = mailbox gate. The kind is written only when the receiving account's intake flag is false; never for an intake mailbox; at most one open proposal of this kind per communication.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">SCOPE = Accept. The request and run are created attributed to the confirming user resolved server-side (the existing caller resolution, fail closed 403); never app-only and never from a client-supplied user id. Existing impersonation rules stay as they are (A5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">SCOPE = request creation. Only through `IntakeRequestSubmitService` with channel Email, regarding the communication, idempotency key `intake-jobb:{reviewLogId}`; no direct Dataverse create in the apply service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = existing proposals. Field-update proposals (all current kinds) keep their exact Apply, Dismiss, Undo and queue-feed behaviour; existing seam tests pass unchanged. The ArchTest pinning `ActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` callers must still pass (do not route the new kind through UpdateRecordAsync).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = proposal text and logs. The proposal label is fixed text plus the request-type label ("Submit as request (NDA review)"); no triage summary, body or obligations copied into the row or logs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = the new kind. Kill switch `Intake:Doors:JobBSuggest:Enabled` (default false) stops new proposals of this kind; open ones still resolve normally.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/communication-intelligence-architecture.md</file>
