      <file>projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/reuse-scan.md (row 9)</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Streaming endpoints" location=".claude/patterns/ai/streaming-endpoints.md">Tag-mapped (ai); no streaming is added.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Public contracts facade" location=".claude/patterns/ai/public-contracts-facade.md">Triage reached only through ICommunicationTriageAi.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Entity operations" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md">sprk_emailreviewlog rows.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Plugin structure" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/plugin-structure.md">Tag-mapped; no plugin added.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files; read `RunEmailProposeAsync`, `ApplyAsync`, `DismissAsync`, the queue-feed projection and the TRIAGE-EMAIL Action's category choices; decide how the kind is encoded on `sprk_emailreviewlog` with existing columns (e.g. target entity `sprk_servicerequest`, a reserved target-field value, proposed value = request type); declare RIGOR FULL, tier opus, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Propose: in `RunEmailProposeAsync`, when the account is not intake, the switch is on, and the triage result's category/outcome maps to a request type, write one proposal of the new kind (skip if one is open).</step>
    <step order="3">Apply: branch on the kind before the field-update path: resolve caller (existing), refuse resolved rows (existing), call `IntakeRequestSubmitService` as the caller, mark the row Applied with the request id. Dismiss: the existing path unchanged.</step>
    <step order="4">Queue feed: ensure the kind appears with its fixed label in the existing `QueueFeedItem` shape.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the criteria; build and run tests incl. ArchTests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the encoding choice and deviations in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the triage result has no category or outcome that can signal "this is a request for legal review", STOP and escalate (adding a choice is an Action/catalog change, ADR-039) rather than adding an AI call or keyword matching on the body.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the new kind cannot be encoded on `sprk_emailreviewlog` without a schema change, or the Exceptions Queue surface cannot render it from the existing `QueueFeedItem` shape, STOP and escalate (shared with the email-intelligence projects).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row 9: `CommunicationProposalApplyService` (Accept/Dismiss/audit), queue feed `CommunicationEndpoints.cs:382`, `ICommunicationTriageAi` (AnalysisServicesModule.cs:632); owner chose the Job B queue over the triage hint. spec New Components row "Job B Submit as request proposal kind".</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended: a new proposal kind on the existing producer, row type, apply/dismiss service and feed; no new surface, endpoint or AI call.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A request emailed to an ordinary (non-intake) mailbox never reaches the pipeline unless the sender re-sends it to the intake mailbox (FR-18).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF, incl. ArchTests</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/Communication/SubmitAsRequestProposalTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplySeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">At a non-intake mailbox with a request signal in the triage result, exactly one open "Submit as request (type)" proposal is written; none at an intake mailbox, none when triage is null, none with the switch off.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no request or run exists for the communication until Accept (FR-18 a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Accept creates exactly one request (channel Email, regarding the communication) and one run attributed to the confirming user; a second Accept creates nothing more (FR-18 b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unresolvable caller gets 403 and nothing is created; an unknown proposal id 404.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dismiss leaves no request and writes exactly one Dismissed audit row (FR-18 c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing field-update proposals pass their existing seam tests unchanged; the ActionSeam caller ArchTest passes (FR-18 d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The proposal row and logs contain no body, summary or obligations text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. One seeding proof for "no request without Accept".</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-18. Dependency on 040 added beyond the brief's 029 because the gate reads 040's intake flag. Run `/conflict-check` (Services/Communication is shared with the email-communication projects).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute (FULL rigor).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
